      "side": 1,
      "message": "No action needed for this comment.  But I wanted to mention that it feels that we should be able to have more descriptive names for `ffi` and `ffi_utils` targets.  But the current names are okay, and I don\u0027t feel strongly about this.  And most importantly I have trouble clearly expressing why I feel better names should be possible:\n\n* One minor concern I have is that `ffi` doesn\u0027t convey that this is a target that Rust crates depend on, and that `ffi_utils` is a target that C++ targets depend on.\n* Maybe one minor change to consider would be to rename the `ffi` target to `skia_rust_common` (matching the `crate_name` seems nice)?",
